id: E6346-draft-2301_80739235
draft: true
title: "HMDFS release handoff needs a content-stream copy across owner boundaries"
category: hmdfs, permissions, w3, release, evidence
match_keywords: >
  HMDFS cp permission denied output pending file_manager mode 0640,
  release handoff owner boundary, tar stream copy, task-private evidence
root_cause: >
  On HarmonyOS PC HMDFS, a task-created output tree can be mapped to the
  file_manager owner with a restrictive mode even when the task shell can cat
  and chmod individual files. cp -R then fails while creating destination
  members, so a successful target result cannot be released or validated.
error_signature: >
  cp: .*output\.pending/.*Permission denied|file_manager.*0640|release_rc=93
trigger_tool: ssh, toybox, hmdfs, w3-controller
phase: w3, release, postrelease, evidence-collection
severity: 2
rec_approach: >
  Keep the consumed run immutable after the ambiguous or failed Release phase.
  In a create-new successor, bind a unique remote root and freeze a release
  helper that creates the task-private destination explicitly, streams file
  contents with tar, verifies the output manifest, and only then moves the
  pending tree into its final evidence path. Keep the original endpoint,
  launch, receipts, and failure record as predecessor evidence.
rec_command: >
  mkdir "$EVIDENCE/output.pending"; (cd "$OUTPUT" && tar -cf - .) |
  (cd "$EVIDENCE/output.pending" && tar -xf -); sha256sum -c
  "$EVIDENCE/output.pending/output-manifest.sha256"; mv output.pending output
verification_cmd: >
  Require the successor controller to report result.status=PASS with all target
  and consumer denominators, Release and PostRelease receipts, output manifest
  verification, collected evidence, frozen validator PASS, and retired=true.
  Read back representative output modes and owner before claiming the fix.
affected_scope: >
  Native OHOS W3 tasks whose evidence or runtime output is created below
  /storage/Users/currentUser or another HMDFS path with service-account owner
  mapping; ordinary local Linux filesystems without the mapping are outside
  this boundary.
safety_boundary: >
  Do not chmod, recopy, release, launch, or delete an already consumed run to
  repair it. A content stream does not replace exact-byte transfer, signature
  checks, receipt-chain validation, or the unique-launch rule. Use only a
  successor remote root and task-owned evidence paths.
doc_file: knowledge/drafts/E6346-draft-2301_80739235.md
last_updated: 2026-09-18
